  "title": "Burial",
  "data": "When the coffin is brought to the grave, it should be set down at the foot end of the grave and then brought towards the grave in three stages. If the dead person is a woman, the coffin should be set down in front of the grave, on the side of the qiblah. Then the dead person's heir, or someone the heir has deputed, may go down into the grave, and while doing so it is recommended to say this supplicatory prayer:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اجْعَلْهَا رَوْضَةً مِنْ رِيَاضِ الْجَنَّةِ وَلَا تَجْعَلْهَا حُفْرَةً مِنْ حُفَرِ النَّارِ\nALLAAHUMMAJ A'LHAA RAWDATAN MIN RIYAADIL JANNATI WA LAA TAJ'ALHAA HUFRATAN MIN HUFARIN NAAR\nO Allah, make it a garden of the gardens of Paradise, and do not make it a pit of the pits of the Fire.\nThe one who buries the dead should go down into the grave barefoot, bareheaded, and with the buttons of his shirt undone. Receiving the body, he should take it down into the grave head first, saying meanwhile:\nبِسْمِ اللّٰهِ وَبِاللّٰهِ وَفِىْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ وَعَلٰى مِلَّةِ رَسُوْلِ اللّٰهِ\nBISMILLAAHI WA BILLAAHI WA FEE SABEELILLAAHI WA A'LAA MILLATI RASOOLILLAAH\nIn the Name of Allah, and by Allah, and in the way of Allah, and upon the creed of the Messenger of Allah.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِيْمَانًا بِكَ وَتَصْدِيْقًا بِكِتَابِكَ هٰذَا مَا وَعَدَنَا اللّٰهُ وَرَسُوْلُهٗ وَصَدَقَ اللّٰهُ وَرَسُوْلُهٗ اَللّٰهُمَّ زِدْنَا اِيْمَانًا وَتَسْلِيْمًا\nALLAAHUMMA EEMAANAN BIKA WA TASDEEQAN BIKITAABIKA HAADHAA MAA WA'ADANALLAAHU WA RASOOLUHOO WA SADAQALLAAHU WA RASOOLUHOO ALLAAHUMMA ZIDNAA EEMAANAN WA TASLEEMAA\nO Allah, (I do this) in faith in You and in belief in Your Book. This is what Allah and His Messenger promised us, and Allah and His Messenger spoke the truth. O Allah, increase us in faith and submission.\nHe should then lay the body on its right side, facing the qiblah, and untie the knots of the shroud at the head and the feet. He should then place the dead person's cheek on the earth. It is recommended to put some soil from the tomb of Imam al-Husayn (a.s.) with the body. He should then line up the bricks over the body, saying meanwhile:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ صِلْ وَحْدَتَهٗ وَاٰنِسْ وَحْشَتَهٗ وَارْحَمْ غُرْبَتَهٗ\nALLAAHUMMA SIL WAHDATAHOO WA AANIS WAHSHATAHOO WARHAM GHURBATAH\nO Allah, keep company with him in his solitude, comfort him in his loneliness, and have mercy on him in his estrangement;\nوَاَسْكِنْ اِلَيْهِ مِنْ رَحْمَتِكَ رَحْمَةً يَسْتَغْنِىْ بِهَا عَنْ رَحْمَةِ مَنْ سِوَاكَ وَاحْشُرْهُ مَعَ مَنْ كَانَ يَتَوَلَّاهُ مِنَ الْاَئِمَّةِ الطَّاهِرِيْنَ\nWA ASKIN ILAYHI MIN RAHMATIKA RAHMATAN YASTAGHNEE BIHAA A'N RAHMATI MAN SIWAAKA WAHSHURHU MA'A MAN KAANA YATAWALLAAHU MINAL A'IMMATIT TAAHIREEN\ngrant him rest with such a mercy from You that he will need no mercy from anyone besides You, and raise him with the pure Imams whom he took as his guardians.\nPrompting the Dead\nBefore lining up the bricks, it is recommended to prompt the dead person with the two testimonies of Islam and the names of the Holy Imams. Addressing the dead person, the prompter should say:\nيَا فُلَانَ بْنَ فُلَانٍ اُذْكُرِ الْعَهْدَ الَّذِىْ خَرَجْتَ عَلَيْهِ مِنْ دَارِ الدُّنْيَا\nYAA FULAANABNA FULAANIN UDHKURIL A'HDAL LADHEE KHARAJTA A'LAYHI MIN DAARID DUNYAA\nO so-and-so, son of so-and-so, remember the covenant with which you left the abode of this world:\nشَهَادَةَ اَنْ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ وَحْدَهٗ لَا شَرِيْكَ لَهٗ وَاَنَّ مُحَمَّدًا عَبْدُهٗ وَرَسُوْلُهٗ وَاَنَّ عَلِيًّا اَمِيْرُ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ وَالْحَسَنَ وَالْحُسَيْنَ\nSHAHAADATA AN LAA ILAAHA ILLALLAAHU WAHDAHOO LAA SHAREEKA LAHOO WA ANNA MUHAMMADAN A'BDUHOO WA RASOOLUHOO WA ANNA A'LIYYAN AMEERUL MU'MINEENA WAL HASANA WAL HUSAYN\nthe testimony that there is no god but Allah, One, having no partner, that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger, and that Ali is the Commander of the Faithful, and al-Hasan and al-Husayn...\nHere the prompter names the rest of the Imams, one by one, and then says:\nاَئِمَّتُكَ اَئِمَّةُ الْهُدَى الْاَبْرَارِ\nA'IMMATUKA A'IMMATUL HUDAL ABRAAR\n...are your Imams, the righteous Imams of guidance.\nIn place of “so-and-so, son of so-and-so”, mention the dead person's name and his father's name. A fuller form of this prompting is given in [Prompting the Dead](I126).\nWhen the bricks have been lined up, the one who buried the dead and all who are present should pour earth over the body, preferably with the backs of their hands, saying meanwhile:\nاِنَّا لِلّٰهِ وَاِنَّاۤ اِلَيْهِ رَاجِعُوْنَ هٰذَا مَا وَعَدَنَا اللّٰهُ وَرَسُوْلُهٗ وَصَدَقَ اللّٰهُ وَرَسُوْلُهٗ اَللّٰهُمَّ زِدْنَا اِيْمَانًا وَتَسْلِيْمًا\nINNAA LILLAAHI WA INNAA ILAYHI RAAJI'OONA HAADHAA MAA WA'ADANALLAAHU WA RASOOLUHOO WA SADAQALLAAHU WA RASOOLUHOO ALLAAHUMMA ZIDNAA EEMAANAN WA TASLEEMAA\nSurely we are Allah's, and to Him we shall surely return. This is what Allah and His Messenger promised us, and Allah and His Messenger spoke the truth. O Allah, increase us in faith and submission."
